The `ArrayUtils.add` method in the Apache Commons Lang library is defined as follows:

```java
public static <T> T[] add(T[] array, T element) {
    Class<?> type;
    if (array != null){
        type = array.getClass();
    } else if (element != null) {
        type = element.getClass();
    } else {
        type = Object.class;
    }
    @SuppressWarnings("unchecked") // type must be T
    T[] newArray = (T[]) copyArrayGrow1(array, type);
    newArray[newArray.length - 1] = element;
    return newArray;
}
```

Based on the failing test case and the current bug report, it seems that the issue lies in the `ArrayUtils.add` method. When both `array` and `element` parameters are `null`, the method returns an `Object[]` array instead of throwing an `IllegalArgumentException`. This behavior can lead to unexpected `ClassCastException`.

To diagnose this issue further and provide a step-by-step explanation, I will need to inspect the implementation of the `ArrayUtils.add` method more closely.

